WEBVTT

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.740
Is there really a ghost?

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.110
Rumor is some people have seen

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.260
a suspicious shadow wandering 
around the hospital.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:15.660
Huh?

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.270
There it is!

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.960
This place became a haunted 
house the second we moved in.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.800
Normally no one would choose 
to live in this creepy place.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.160
That's what makes it a good hideout.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.620
Whoops.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.430
Huh?

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.760
What is that?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.390
An Umbra's about to be born.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.370
Born?

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:45.060
Umbra are born from human imagination.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.440
When a lot of people imagine something,
 it takes shape.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.260
It's afraid?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.940
It's a jack-o'-lantern.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:54.900
Leave it.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:56.710
Hey.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.560
Don't be scared.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.240
Come here.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.030
I'm in no position to say this,

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:14.380
but no good ever comes from Umbra 
and humans associating with each other.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:18.580
Who decided that?

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.540
<i>And now, listen to this.</i>

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.020
<i>This is Roland Lee performing...</i>

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:07.370
<b>Episode 5 The Fairy's Lover</b>

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.410
Did Ton say she'd be the manager?

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.500
Yeah.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.250
We have a new associate.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.500
Did she finish changing?

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.800
Tada!

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.430
Well? How do I look?

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.470
You're so cute.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.720
Hey, nice.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.220
It suits you well.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:23.740
Sheesh!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.850
You're supposed to compliment 
me, even if you have to lie.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.140
This is a lie, but it looks very good on you.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.140
You are supremely beautiful right now.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.400
Good.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.700
You're really okay with that?

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:41.570
My parents told me to go to school in China.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:45.990
I defied their wishes by coming here, 
so I want to pay for my own tuition.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.040
So, what does the manager do?

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.790
Interacting with customers, setting tables, 
shopping, and taking out the garbage.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.400
And washing dishes.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.960
Those are just odd jobs.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.530
You're less than Wayne.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.970
What?

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.600
What a beautiful woman.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:05.390
Welcome.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.810
I'd like a sun and moon blended tea.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.980
We don't serve that here.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.150
My friend who lives in the Tower 
of London told me about this place.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.040
Excuse me.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.540
This way, please.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.080
Go ahead.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:31.750
So this is how it works.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.920
Go on. It's your first customer.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.620
I'm Ton, the manager.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.340
You must have a request for us.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:45.300
Yes. I want you to find me a gentleman 
who will make my heart flutter.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.240
Uh, you mean...?

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.220
As quickly as possible, please.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.980
Um, that seat is for clients with 
requests relating to Umbra.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.990
That's fine.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.100
After all, I'm an Umbra.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.020
What?

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.620
It's not a problem, is it?

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.330
She's a leannán sídhe.

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:03.650
Leannán sídhe?

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:07.240
I'm Lydia, and I'm seeking 
a romantic partner.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:08.820
Will you take the job?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.170
Uh...

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.410
Yes, understood.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:13.370
What?!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.540
A romantic request is such a wonderful thing.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.280
Thank you.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.130
Ton, I've written my preferences here.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.120
I'll come again in three days.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.860
Tall with well-defined features.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.560
Enjoys the occasional drink.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.930
Possesses talent and passion 
for the arts. Blood type O.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.350
This is rather specific.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.300
What are we going to do?

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.860
Find her a partner.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.820
Surely Umbra fall in love, right?

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.100
That's not the problem.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:46.660
What?

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:49.440
Leannán sídhe are Umbra birthed

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.410
from the rumor that talented artists die young.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.250
They're fairies who take 
their victim's vitality

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.690
in exchange for success, 
eventually killing them.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.580
In other words, today's job is...

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:04.590
A request to find her the perfect victim.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.470
I'm going to turn her down.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.600
It's too late.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.550
Why don't you tell her the
next time she comes?

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.700
It's our shop's policy not to 
reject a job we've accepted.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:17.230
What?

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.660
Why don't you find her 
someone who's hard to kill?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.230
Nobody like that exists!

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.330
No, I know just the man.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.440
You want to introduce me to a woman?

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:31.880
A-A friend of mine asked me 
introduce them to someone,

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:36.840
but I don't know anyone 
decent in London, so...

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.670
So Vlad thought you'd be a good choice.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.820
I appreciate the offer, but since you guys 
are involved it's all a bit suspicious.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.820
Luxurious and beautiful blonde hair.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.260
Eyes as blue as the summer sky.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.010
I've seen her. She's incredibly beautiful.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:56.500
If she's so pretty, I'm sure men 
will approach her without my help.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.770
No one wants to be approached 
based on their appearance alone.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.380
If you feel like meeting her,

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:01.940
come to our place the night 
of the day after tomorrow.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.580
Excuse me.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:08.050
It's me. What's up?

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.030
What? What are you talking about?

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.520
The explosion in the market 
the other day was an accident.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.240
How has anyone been arrested?

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:17.840
Who is he? Sheesh.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.540
Excuse me...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.540
Yeah, I get it.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.710
I'll be there if I feel like it.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.420
Th-Thank you.

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.960
It feels like we're doing a bad thing.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:33.180
Detective Gregory is looking 
for Shinyao, isn't he?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.760
Don't worry.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.990
Based on that reaction, I doubt he'll come.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.190
Today's the day they're 
supposed to come, right?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.560
Yeah. I doubt he's coming now.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:48.850
I'm glad.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:51.210
It's not good to trick people.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:52.350
We didn't trick him.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:55.470
We just didn't tell him she's an Umbra 
who sucks the life out of people.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:57.340
That's exactly the problem.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:59.270
You came.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.390
Welcome.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.360
Blended tea.

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.850
Very well.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:11.100
Thank you for making time in your 
busy schedule to come today.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:11.970
Don't worry about it.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.660
As luck would have it,
 I didn't have any real work to do today.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:20.320
Anyway, since I don't have any 
real work to do, I'm avail—

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.980
I'm available.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:28.440
It doesn't seem like he is.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.290
And he acted like he wasn't interested.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:32.860
She's here.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.710
This is George Gregory.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:42.430
He is—

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:44.310
Toryu, I'll take it from here.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:44.880
Yes, sir.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.500
May I ask your name?

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.100
It's Lydia.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.970
This is unexpected,

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.550
but someone like you might 
be surprisingly interesting.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:08:58.990
I see. That's...

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:02.180
I see, I see.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.370
I'm scared things seem to be going well.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:08.960
It won't.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:09.690
Huh?

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.600
I'm glad you agreed to meet me today.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.640
I was promised I'd be introduced 
to a wonderful man.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:19.170
And I was told a beautiful 
woman would be coming.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:20.030
Really?

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.410
No one told me she'd be an Umbra, though.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.560
Sorry, but I've still got work to do.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.020
I'm leaving.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.590
Wait, wait, wait!

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.750
I'm assigned to Umbra crimes.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.170
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:36.120
Do you have a problem with her?

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.970
It's in every fairy tale 
from all over the world.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:42.470
Umbra and humans can never be happy together.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.580
Sorry, but I'm leaving.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.620
I knew this wouldn't work.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.610
If you want to meet someone,
 isn't there someplace else you should go?

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:55.870
I already tried.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:59.030
Want me to find someone else for you?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.240
Thanks, but—

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.570
Leave it to me.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:04.060
I'll find someone close 
to what you requested.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.330
Now, then...

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.420
Time to show her what I can do.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:15.950
<i>Let's see.</i>

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.410
<i>Here's one. He's a perfect 
match for her criteria.</i>

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.770
<i>But he's that musician 
who's been in the news.</i>

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.520
I'm sorry.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.650
It was a bad idea to hide
 the fact you're an Umbra.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.730
But he wouldn't have even 
come if you'd told him.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:36.860
Shall I make you something?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.220
Something that will lift my spirits, please.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.540
You got it.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.430
So she's the great-granddaughter 
of that famous Umbra hunter, huh?

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:53.710
She's quite cute.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.070
But far from being a lady.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.810
Oh, really?

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:01.580
What is it?

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.730
You're quite a catch, aren't you?

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:05.010
Thank you.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.180
And the cook is cheerful.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:09.160
I bet being around him would cheer me up.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:10.270
He's just a dog.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:11.980
And then there's the waiter.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.390
His sincerity shows through in his work.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.110
His earnestness is his only strength.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:18.320
Maybe I'll choose from one of you.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.570
That's an interesting suggestion.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:25.120
Don't you think it could 
work out between two Umbra?

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:29.140
It's impossible for an Umbra 
and human to be together.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:32.170
Lydia!

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.310
Roland.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:35.420
Why?

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:36.680
Huh?

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:50.560
I searched all the images 
I could find online.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.230
That's how I found the perfect match.

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:54.620
That's him.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.220
Roland Lee, huh?

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.260
He's a recently popular singer.

00:11:58.260 --> 00:11:59.650
He's even in the paper.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:04.780
After the paparazzi caught him with a woman, 
he's been hospitalized for mysterious reasons.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.250
When I sent Roland 
a picture of Lydia,

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.340
he instantly responded 
that he wanted to see her.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.460
We've already broken up.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.630
So they're exes?

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:19.810
I've been looking for you ever since.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.280
Why did you leave me?

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:25.140
You'll be ruined if I stay
 with you any longer.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:26.810
Who cares about the tabloids?

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:27.930
I'm an artist!

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:29.720
Is this her in the photo?

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.730
I've worked to prove myself through my music.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.470
It's not like that.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.030
At this rate, you'll...

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:36.770
We should stop.

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:37.800
Lydia.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.070
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.330
Lydia!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:52.790
You don't seem to be feeling well.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:53.870
Yeah.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.120
Were you together for a long time?

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.120
It's been almost five years.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.270
We met on the street,
before I became successful.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.360
It was love at first sight for both of us.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:08.350
Maybe that's why it was so surprising 
when she said she wanted to end things.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.030
It was the right call.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:13.460
If you stay with her any longer, you'll die.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:20.350
Unless you find a new love, 
you'll never be able to leave Roland.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:23.150
That's why you wanted to fall in love again.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:27.330
Even if we're apart, as long as we love
each other, I'll continue taking his vitality.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.030
It's even worse when we're together.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.490
You really do love him.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.750
I knew it was wrong.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.100
Strange, isn't it?

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.920
Not only did I fall in love 
with a human as an Umbra,

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:43.670
but I don't want to take his vitality.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:49.400
I think falling in love is a wonderful thing.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:52.180
It's not strange that things have changed.

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:56.520
But because of my love, he's dying.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:02.640
Ton, you're the great-granddaughter 
of a famous Umbra hunter.

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.280
Yes.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.860
Then you could kill me.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:10.520
I'm willing to sacrifice everything, so—

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:11.230
But—

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:14.230
An Umbra and a human can never be together.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.000
That's not true!

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.080
I know.

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:20.500
There may be a way in my 
great-grandmother's study.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.520
You saw his face.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.380
He doesn't have a moment to spare.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.500
But it's worth a shot.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.480
Don't you agree?

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.720
Ton, promise me this.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:38.270
When he's reached his limit...

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.020
Let's do this.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.090
Welcome.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.840
Thank you for coming despite the rain.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.890
It's all right. More importantly,

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.210
judging by your expression, 
it didn't go well.

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:17.100
No, we should still have time.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.780
You promised.

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:23.540
Roland!

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.610
Hey, Lydia.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.270
Why?

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.740
Vlad told me to come tonight.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.450
Lydia, they told me everything.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.540
You're just an Umbra.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.370
You don't care about human life.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.800
Sorry, but I'm an Umbra 
second and a man first.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:46.490
Lydia!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.000
It's an emergency!

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:53.160
Don't.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.840
His life's in danger.

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:55.710
So, what?

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:56.930
So, what?

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:00.890
Haven't you ever had something 
more valuable than your life?

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:03.690
You're immortal. Don't talk 
to me about the value of life.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.240
Let go!

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:09.190
No.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:12.140
At first I thought you didn't like the media.

00:16:12.140 --> 00:16:13.660
I was willing to give up singing for you.

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:19.180
I wondered if it was because
 I couldn't get out of bed anymore.

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:22.240
But that wasn't it.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:23.840
That's right.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.440
I'm your grim reaper.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:27.620
I don't care.

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.190
Your heart hasn't left me yet.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:34.470
If anything, it's still concerned for me.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:37.420
Just one more minute. One more second.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:40.890
I couldn't ask for anything 
greater than being here with you.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.270
Stop.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:42.810
I love—

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.070
Don't!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:46.240
I'm finding someone new!

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:50.700
I can't be with someone who 
selfishly ignores what I want!

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:52.680
Stop forcing your love on me!

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.740
Do you want me to kill you?

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.050
That's the worst kind of self-satisfaction!

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:03.050
What am I supposed to do?

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.710
Shouldn't we go after them?

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.310
Let him die.

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:10.840
What?

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.690
Dying in the arms of the woman he loves

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:16.120
is worth more than a 
hundred years of solitude.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:21.180
Lydia, I love you.

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:24.140
I'll love you forever.

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:30.300
Ton, you remember our promise.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:31.600
Yes.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:37.530
I'm sorry. This is all I can do.

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:40.260
Thank you, Ton.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.840
Lydia?

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:53.700
What are you...?

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.340
Y-You're not... Don't!

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:58.160
Let me...

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:01.570
Roland, I love you.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.520
I'll love you forever and ever.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.620
When I decided to go to school in London,

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.580
I thought I'd be starting my own life.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:53.480
But that's a very difficult and scary thing.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:57.740
You mean the responsibility 
that comes with your decisions.

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:02.840
When I make a decision,
 it affects the people around me.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.450
I'm responsible for that.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:07.160
Do you regret what happened?

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:13.290
No. But I wonder if there 
was a better answer.

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:17.320
Lady Rijan was forced to 
use the Artemis armlet

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:21.550
on Umbra who were experiencing 
special circumstances.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:24.930
"Roland Lee Resurrection?"

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:31.230
The Artemis armlet transforms those 
you want to save into amethysts.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:35.680
I believe you made the best possible choice.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:41.520
They can't communicate or see each other,

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:44.530
but the souls they loved are there.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.120
You granted them their greatest wish.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:49.840
We couldn't have done it without you.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.150
You should be proud.

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:52.890
Thanks.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:00.720
Is it really so difficult for Umbra 
and humans to love each other?

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.550
Ton, don't worry about it.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:04.390
Huh?

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:06.220
Just give it a try.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.470
Wh-What are you...

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.720
Just kidding.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:17.490
What was that for? Jeez!

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:25.400
<i>Here's the new song he released 
alongside his return.</i>

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:29.640
<i>This is Roland Lee performing 
"The Fairy's Lover."</i>

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:05.410
Welcome back, sir.

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:07.130
Have you found Haysin?

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:08.870
No, not yet.

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:10.990
I'm holding a meeting to discuss 
countermeasures in ten minutes.

00:22:10.990 --> 00:22:12.260
Gather the other members.

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:12.960
Yes, sir.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:17.400
London's fallen into chaos while I was gone.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:24.130
I shall bring happiness to people, 
bring light to the world,

00:22:24.130 --> 00:22:28.200
and cast a light so bright 
it erases all shadows.

00:22:28.430 --> 00:22:32.270
I, Van Helsing, so swear on my name.

00:22:35.160 --> 00:23:32.050
<b>Phantom 
Twilight Plus</b>

00:22:35.780 --> 00:22:37.320
Phantom in the Twilight Plus!

00:22:38.880 --> 00:22:42.090
It's time to introduce the 
final member of the Twilights.

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:43.560
I'm Wayne King.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:46.420
I'm always hanging around as a mannequin.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:48.880
Wayne, you're a ghost without a body, right?

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:49.710
Probably.

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:52.350
I don't have any memories, 
so things are a bit hazy.

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.340
Well, whatever.

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:56.770
Even if we knew what you were,
 it wouldn't be very useful information.

00:22:56.770 --> 00:22:58.730
Your introductions are as sloppy as ever!

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:01.450
It just means you're better 
now than you used to be.

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:04.850
You've got the handy power 
to possess any nearby objects

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:07.070
and manipulate them as you see fit.

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:07.810
That's right.

00:23:07.810 --> 00:23:11.000
When I possess electronics, 
I can easily hack them.

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:13.950
I might actually be the most 
useful member of the Twilights.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:15.230
What was that?

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:17.300
Are you picking a fight with me?

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:19.010
Then I'm not giving you a handicap!

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:21.540
Don't! I don't have any combat abilities!

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.670
But even though you've possessed a mannequin,

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:26.410
you shouldn't be able to speak or eat.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:29.180
That's because, uh... I don't know...

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:30.520
Magic?

00:23:30.520 --> 00:23:34.220
Can we stop explaining 
everything away with magic?

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:50.200
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:38.850
A new enemy appears before 
the Twilights: Van Helsing.

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:42.540
The man who inherited the name of the 
legendary vampire hunter in the modern age

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.900
proclaims his love for humans and 
hatred for Umbra as he hunts us down.

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:50.200
<b>Episode 6 Midnight Sun</b>

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:49.740
Next time: Midnight Sun.
